  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "lapsed_date": "21/08/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;The outbuilding&#x27;s foundation and sub-structure within the Root Protection Area (RPA) of the retained trees shall be implemented in strict accordance with the following requirements: Foundation Type: The foundation for the outbuilding shall be constructed with hand tools only, using screw piles. No mechanical excavation, traditional strip foundations, continuous beams, or trenching shall be used within the RPA of retained trees onsite or in neighbouring gardens. Gaseous Exchange: The finished sub-structure shall be a suspended ground floor/slab creating a ventilated air space between the underside of the structure and the existing soil surface to ensure: Soil Hydrology: The design should encourage the natural movement and infiltration of rainfall into the soil beneath the structure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To safeguard the long-term health, stability, and viability of the retained tree(s) by minimising soil disturbance in accordance with the principles of BS 5837:2012 &quot;Trees in relation to design, demolition and construction – Recommendations&quot;, to accord with the requirements of Section 197(a) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 and in the interests of visual amenity, having regard to Policy LP51 in the Local Plan 2033 (adopted 2020).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
